hat enable seamless, scalable data orchestration for our customers' tech stacks. \n \n \n Own end-to-end delivery of backend features and services, from design through deployment and monitoring. \n \n \n Contribute to our integration infrastructure, building reusable patterns and tooling that make adding new integrations faster and more reliable. \n \n \n Collaborate with frontend, product, and design teams to deliver high-quality customer experiences backed by robust backend systems. \n \n \n Requirements: \n \n \n 4-6 years of backend engineering experience with a track record of shipping reliable, well-tested systems. \n \n \n Strong fundamentals in backend development, including API design, data modeling, concurrent systems, and performance optimization. \n \n \n Experience working with relational databases and distributed systems concepts. \n \n \n Curious and eager to learn - you're excited to dig into unfamiliar systems, understand complex integrations, and grow your technical skills. \n \n \n Bias toward action and ownership - you see a problem, propose solutions, and drive it to completion without needing constant direction. \n \n \n Strong communication skills and comfort working cross-functionally with product, design, and other engineers. \n \n \n Thrive in fast-paced environments with evolving priorities and high autonomy. \n \n \n Interest and experience with AI tools and prompting - you leverage AI in your workflow and can help level up the team's capabilities. \n \n \n You'll stand out if you have: \n \n \n Experience building integrations, ETL pipelines, or working with third-party APIs at scale. \n \n \n Exposure to financial services, fintech, or B2B SaaS products. \n \n \n Experience at seed/early-stage startups where you wore multiple hats and moved quickly. \n \n \n Familiarity with event-driven architectures, message queues, or data synchronization patterns. \n \n \n Previously built side projects or contributed to open source software. \n \n 